# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Caddy reverse proxy — clean https:// names for every web UI.
#
#  These use the *.home.lan domain with Caddy's INTERNAL CA (self-signed),
#  which is ideal for LAN + Tailscale access. Two things make it work:
#    1. A local DNS record so the names resolve to this server. Easiest:
#       AdGuard Home > Filters > DNS rewrites > add  *.home.lan -> <server-ip>
#    2. Trust Caddy's root CA on your devices (optional, removes the browser
#       warning). Grab it from: ${CONFIG_ROOT}/caddy/data/caddy/authorities/local/root.crt
#
#  Prefer real public HTTPS instead? Replace `tls internal` with your email
#  at the top and use real domains (needs public DNS + open 80/443, or the
#  Cloudflare / DNS-challenge plugin). See README.
#
#  Container names below are the compose service names — Caddy reaches them
#  over the shared Docker network. qBittorrent is published via `gluetun`.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

(lan) {
	tls internal
}

jellyfin.home.lan {
	import lan
	reverse_proxy jellyfin:8096
}

